    "code_released": "https://github.com/hilhert/CSP",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The reported task data are dynamically regenerated rather than a fixed small training set, so they do not establish overfitting followed by delayed generalization. The paper does not report a training-set-size sweep. Some training-dynamics statements are textual descriptions of figures rather than tabulated epoch-by-epoch values. Results are averaged over five seeds, with notable seed sensitivity for CSP.",
    "rows_left_out": "The main length-generalization table reports additional L = 16 and L = 32 values (and appendix tables report L = 48, selected per-seed values, and standard deviations); these were omitted in favor of the L = 64 extrapolation results. No result-bearing condition is omitted for a version tested, because no version is directly tested.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No fixed small dataset, no train-saturation then test-jump timeline, and no training-set-size sweep."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "No mechanistic progress measures and no account of memorizing components being removed."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "No non-algorithmic data and no manipulation of initialization scale or weight norm."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No LLM pretraining or fine-tuning."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "Weight decay is fixed, not varied. No critical dataset size and no ungrokking."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "Learned algorithms are not identified or compared across runs; seed variance concerns length-generalization accuracy only."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "No controlled test of optimizer or floating-point artifacts as a cause of delayed generalization."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "The paper contains internal inconsistencies. Weight decay is given as 1e-7 in Section 3.1 but 1e-4 in Appendix E.3. The Figure 5 caption claims perfect CSP mod-3 accuracy for seed 45, but Table 3 gives CSP-Vanilla 0.826 and CSP-Fast 0.746 for seed 45 at L=64. Table 1 CSP-Vanilla L=32 values (parity 0.922, mod-3 0.980) differ from the Appendix means (0.970, 0.965). The abstract's claim of nearly 100% mod-3 accuracy at L=64 exceeds the reported mean of 0.927. None of these affect the grokking verdict."
  },
